From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: split advertised AKM suites by haul, not by iftype
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

The AKM Suite Capabilities TLV (17.2.78, Table 101) carries Num_BackAKM for
the backhaul BSSes and Num_FrontAKM for the fronthaul ones. A fronthaul BSS is
an AP as well, so keying the split off the AP/STA interface type puts the same
list in both fields. 999999-akm-suites-from-ap-sections merged every AP on the
radio into one bitmap and used it for both, which did exactly that.

Our fronthaul runs sae-mixed and our backhaul runs sae, so the merged bitmap
told every peer that our backhaul speaks PSK. It does not.

Measured on the wire 2026-09-03 (tcpdump -i any 'ether proto 0x893a' on the
controller, triggered with query_ap_caps), CMDU 0x8002 from a live agent:

  Num_BackAKM  = 2   00:0f:ac:02 (PSK)   00:0f:ac:08 (SAE)
  Num_FrontAKM = 2   00:0f:ac:02 (PSK)   00:0f:ac:08 (SAE)

with uci apmld_bh.encryption='sae' - no PSK on that BSS at all. A peer that
believes this and offers PSK on the backhaul gets nothing back, and will look
for the fault on its own side. Advertising nothing would have been more honest
than advertising what we do not offer.

netif_apcfg already carries the haul: multi_ap is 0x01 backhaul, 0x02
fronthaul, 0x03 combined, and the rest of the agent keys off it the same way
(agent_map.c:2371). Fill the two bitmaps separately from it.

The upstream field names read backwards here and are left alone:
agent_gen_akm_suite_cap() emits ap_akms as Num_BackAKM and sta_akms as
Num_FrontAKM. Filling them by haul keeps that mapping intact and corrects only
what goes in - nothing else in the tree reads either array.

--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -3944,7 +3944,7 @@
 					       struct wifi_radio_element *re)
 {
 	struct netif_apcfg *apcfg;
-	uint16_t enc = 0;
+	uint16_t bh_enc = 0, fh_enc = 0;
 
 	/* Encryption is a property of the BSS, not of the radio. The radio
 	 * sections carry no encryption option at all - every one of them
@@ -3952,18 +3952,45 @@
 	 * the AKM Suite Capabilities TLV went out empty, leaving no peer able
 	 * to learn what security this device speaks.
 	 *
-	 * Merge every AP on this radio: one radio can host BSSes with
-	 * different security, and the TLV advertises what the device can do.
+	 * Split by haul, not by interface type. The TLV (17.2.78, Table 101)
+	 * carries Num_BackAKM for the backhaul BSSes and Num_FrontAKM for the
+	 * fronthaul ones; a fronthaul BSS is an AP too, so keying off AP/STA
+	 * puts the same list in both fields. Merging every AP on the radio did
+	 * exactly that, and since our fronthaul runs sae-mixed while the
+	 * backhaul runs sae, we ended up telling every peer that our backhaul
+	 * speaks PSK. It does not.
+	 *
+	 * Measured on the wire 2026-09-03, CMDU 0x8002 from a live agent:
+	 *   Num_BackAKM  = 2   00:0f:ac:02 (PSK)   00:0f:ac:08 (SAE)
+	 *   Num_FrontAKM = 2   00:0f:ac:02 (PSK)   00:0f:ac:08 (SAE)
+	 * with uci apmld_bh.encryption='sae' - no PSK anywhere on that BSS.
+	 * A peer that believes it and offers PSK on the backhaul gets nothing,
+	 * and will look for the fault on its own side. Advertising nothing is
+	 * more honest than advertising what we do not offer.
+	 *
+	 * Note the field names below are the upstream ones and read backwards
+	 * here: agent_gen_akm_suite_cap() emits ap_akms as Num_BackAKM and
+	 * sta_akms as Num_FrontAKM. Filling them by haul keeps that mapping
+	 * intact and only corrects what goes in.
 	 */
 	list_for_each_entry(apcfg, &a->cfg.aplist, list) {
+		uint16_t apenc;
+
 		if (strncmp(apcfg->device, re->name, sizeof(apcfg->device)))
 			continue;
-		enc |= get_encryption(apcfg->encryption);
+
+		apenc = get_encryption(apcfg->encryption);
+
+		/* multi_ap: 0x01 backhaul, 0x02 fronthaul, 0x03 combined */
+		if (apcfg->multi_ap & 0x01)
+			bh_enc |= apenc;
+		if (apcfg->multi_ap & 0x02)
+			fh_enc |= apenc;
 	}
 
-	re->num_ap_akms = default_akm_suites_from_encryption(enc,
+	re->num_ap_akms = default_akm_suites_from_encryption(bh_enc,
 			(uint8_t *)re->ap_akms, MAX_AKM_SUITES);
-	re->num_sta_akms = default_akm_suites_from_encryption(enc,
+	re->num_sta_akms = default_akm_suites_from_encryption(fh_enc,
 			(uint8_t *)re->sta_akms, MAX_AKM_SUITES);
 }
 
